  "body": "## October 30 authorized CI activation \u2014 HOLD\n\nRepository Actions is now enabled for the existing Pull Request Tests workflow. All six specified operational workflows remain disabled; read-only token defaults and disabled automated PR approval are unchanged.\n\nIndependent GitHub CI failed:\n- PR #44, head `922f1f8f8c66ef14674eb9aa20db144a45dada68`, tested merge `183398e54172058472184f1704f32c4cda8033a4`: **764 passed, 5 failed, 157.49s**. [Run 41060138183](https://github.com/JCRABURN/cfb-betting-system-v3/actions/runs/41060138183).\n- PR #45, head `6e1948dd9b675a3f1226350ce5b40a6556e09f7a`, tested merge `295456f93c6fdfcfcf2d65b9f61d73733ca319a2`: **803 passed, 6 failed, 165.43s**. [Run 41060143806](https://github.com/JCRABURN/cfb-betting-system-v3/actions/runs/41060143806).\n\nBoth ran on Ubuntu 26.04 / Python 3.11.17. Safety and migration gates passed. Week 7 diagnostic replay, Week 8 audit/research replay, and additionally PR #45 Week 9 context replay failed. Exact mismatch causes remain unresolved; earlier Windows passes do not override these failures. Logs and configuration receipts are retained locally in the CI merge-gates worktree under `outputs/2026-ci-merge-gates/20261030-authorized-activation/`; no new source push or rerun follows the stop condition.\n\nAll 125 protected artifact hashes and the source database hash still match. No application/model/policy/security changes beyond the explicitly authorized activation; no operational run, merge or approval. **HOLD #44, #45 and #46** pending a valid repair, successful exact-tree GitHub CI and an independent non-author APPROVED review. No independent reviewer has been designated. #46 has no independent run.\n\n---\n\nPrior description retained below for provenance; the October 30 CI failure status above supersedes earlier CI status statements.\n\nGrades all 52 ATS and 52 totals from PR #42's pregame seal against independently reconciled ESPN and CFBD scores. ATS: 26\u201326; totals: 23\u201329. Adds deterministic ledgers, Weeks 5\u20138 diagnostic tables, validated scoring-sequence review and numerical proposals labeled RESEARCH ONLY. CLV remains INCOMPLETE; no Week 8 owner approval is invented.\n\nExact audit head: **922f1f8f8c66ef14674eb9aa20db144a45dada68**. Dependencies are repaired aggregate #41 \u2192 #42. #43 is a sibling Week 9 ingest branch after #42, not a prerequisite for this audit; dependent #45 contains both #43 and #44. Do not merge defective ancestors without the #41 repairs.\n\nFiles: five new audit/capture/research scripts, tests/test_week8_postgame_audit.py, two evidence directories, docs/WEEK8_POSTGAME_ENGINEERING.md and additive .gitattributes rules. No schema, dependency, production model, weekly policy or historical artifact changes. Writers fail closed on existing output; verifiers require exact checksum coverage, consistent statuses and deterministic output bytes.\n\nFresh independent-checkout verification on October 29, using this exact PR head: **769 passed, 39 existing warnings, 195.39 seconds, exit 0**. HEAD before/after and clean tracked diffs are recorded. This is local Windows Python 3.12.14 execution, not GitHub CI. Eight read-only gates also pass. The separate #45 exact-head integration run passed 809 tests in 210.81s; these are distinct runs, not substitutions.\n\nExecuted with repository .venv Python:\n```text\npython -m pytest -q\npython scripts/verify_repo_safety.py\npython -m scripts.verify_migrations\npython -m scripts.verify_cloud_migrations\npython -m scripts.verify_week7_audit_integrity\npython -m scripts.seal_week8_board --verify\npython -m scripts.build_week8_postgame_audit --verify\npython -m scripts.week8_scoring_sequence_review --verify\npython -m scripts.week8_numerical_research --verify\n```\n\nAll 104 picks reconcile; all 57 audit evidence files and 47 protected sources verify. All 52 scoring sequences validate. No selected-side backdoor covers meet the existing final-five-minutes definition; original conservative classifications remain preserved. One kickoff discrepancy is recorded separately without altering the frozen schedule. Original source DB SHA256 remains 09d0bcda684356001bacf8bc9e42939add56b053f405564d9be924e39c0cf842.\n\nCI root cause is now established: authenticated GET actions/permissions returned **enabled:false**, although CI workflow 328094886 is active and PR-open events exist. There are zero recorded GitHub runs/checks/statuses. Main has no branch protection/rulesets; none were changed. Read-only token defaults and disabled automated PR approvals remain intact. Owner authorization is required for the documented plan to disable non-CI workflows before enabling repository Actions. No workflow was duplicated or security setting changed.\n\n**HOLD.** Exact-head local tests and integrity gates pass, but independent GitHub CI and an independent approving reviewer remain outstanding. The only listed collaborator is author JCRABURN; the existing COMMENTED review is not APPROVED. No approval or merge is performed.\n\nLimitations: missing timestamp-qualified historical closes; no owner-approved Week 8 five; retrospective Week 5\u20136 ranking evidence; small, correlated samples. Missing historical CLV alone does not block unrelated integrity code. The native aggregate whitespace check includes a trailing-space line in checksum-pinned audit code and historical evidence; those bytes are preserved, not silently reformatted. PR #46 supplies a separate explanation and clean PDF reading copies without suppressing findings.\n\n[Fresh #44/#45 verification and provenance](https://github.com/JCRABURN/cfb-betting-system-v3/blob/8631d45f3bfed387f793aa86cccf2886fde8c7a4/outputs/2026-ci-merge-gates/20261029-investigation/FINAL_VERIFICATION.md) \u00b7 [Full CI investigation](https://github.com/JCRABURN/cfb-betting-system-v3/blob/8631d45f3bfed387f793aa86cccf2886fde8c7a4/docs/CI_MERGE_GATE_RECONCILIATION.md) \u00b7 [Preserved prior PR descriptions](https://github.com/JCRABURN/cfb-betting-system-v3/blob/8631d45f3bfed387f793aa86cccf2886fde8c7a4/outputs/2026-ci-merge-gates/20261029-investigation/pr-descriptions-before-ci-reconciliation.json)\n\nRollback: leave this audit unmerged or revert only its additive changes while retaining custody evidence. Migration checks use disposable copies; no source DB regeneration or recovery is needed. No original repository, NFL work, secrets or unrelated files changed. v2.8 remains unchanged.",
